bulary/images/sofa.webp","1","A complete sentence starts with a capital letter; a capital later in the sentence cannot replace it.","Ada","Discriminate a complete CVC word against real CVC neighbours; the printed initial alone does not distinguish the key.","Recognize sentence-initial capitalisation in one complete simple thought; no sentence repair or paragraph judgment is required.","Recognize the conventional capitalized form of one supplied name.","bottle","catch","checking the clock","climb","cry","dance","dim","drawing a line","eat","first_word","folding the blanket","here","hfw-word:all","hfw-word:an","hfw-word:and","hfw-word:are","hfw-word:as","hfw-word:be","hfw-word:but","hfw-word:by","hfw-word:day","hfw-word:did","hfw-word:do","hfw-word:for","hfw-word:get","hfw-word:go","hfw-word:had","hfw-word:has","hfw-word:he","hfw-word:her","hfw-word:him","hfw-word:his","hfw-word:how","hfw-word:if","hfw-word:may","hfw-word:my","hfw-word:no","hfw-word:not","hfw-word:now","hfw-word:or","hfw-word:out","hfw-word:see","hfw-word:she","hfw-word:so","hfw-word:was","hfw-word:we","job","kit","last_word","laugh","point","relevance","return_sweep","scared — afraid","scared — angry","scared — brave","scared — lonely","smile","sneeze","stretch","throw","wag","wash","way","“four” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.",20,"/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/boat-98d7ed596e.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/mop-e235065535.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/mud-63ab413311.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/mug-056f8accc6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/pin-4ab29fc75d.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/rug-433a599821.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/sheep-22771498fa.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/sock-c00268dd15.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/ten-43d174c3c5.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/tin-7a4f7e9ba9.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/van-81002e64c7.mp3","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-hug.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/glass.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/jam.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/jet.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/in/pin-02.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/cot.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/peach.webp","A","Ada hung the picture list above her own head. The younger children could not see what to collect. She crouched beside them, noticed the shelf in their way, and moved the list down where they could see it.","Alma poured paint onto a mixing plate and then went to find a brush and water. The paint dried while she searched. Before her next painting she put the brush, water and plate together, then poured the paint.","Amir took a blue coat from the hook because it looked like his. Its owner came looking for it. Amir checked the name inside and returned it. Then he checked another blue coat and found his own name.","Asha moved the meeting blanket from the tree to the porch when rain began. Her friend kept waiting under the tree. Asha went back and explained the change. Her friend brought his bag to the dry porch.","Bela chose shiny thin paper for the base of her model because it looked special. The base bent under the model. She tried a plain stiff sheet, which held the model level, and used that sheet for the base.","Bo heard that a parcel belonged by the side door. He put it beside the playground door, but the collector waited elsewhere. Bo asked which side door was meant, then moved it to the door beside the office.","Eli tried to learn a long drum pattern all at once and kept losing his place. He practiced its first short part, then the next part. After joining the practiced parts, he could play the pattern through.","Ellis checked one wheel on the model bus and said the bus was ready. A different wheel stuck when he pushed it. He turned every wheel by hand, freed the stuck one, and tried the bus again.","Finn glued a handle onto a cardboard basket and lifted it at once. The wet joint slid apart. He glued it again and left it flat until the joint was firm. This time the handle stayed on.","Grace made a tiny book pocket for her partner without asking which book it would hold. The book was too wide. She asked to see the book and made a wider pocket that held it.","Imani wrapped bright paper around every part of her toy cart. The paper jammed between a wheel and the frame. She cut the paper away from the moving wheel. The cart rolled again.","Jo kept the game scores in her head. After a break she could not remember which team had seven points. On the next game she marked every point on a scorecard. The teams could check the score after the break.","Kai used a wide cup to pour beads into a narrow bottle. Beads bounced onto the floor. He held a funnel in the neck and poured through it. The beads went into the bottle.","Luca piled beans above the rim of a small tray. They spilled whenever he moved it. He divided them between two trays, leaving space below each rim. He carried both trays without losing beans.","Maya kept wiping water from under a plant pot. The puddle returned whenever she watered it because its tray was cracked. She replaced the tray. After the next watering, the shelf stayed dry.","Mira painted every paper flag before trying the new paint. When the flags dried, the paint cracked. She tried a little paint on spare paper, chose one that stayed smooth, and made the flags again.","Noor tied the ribbon tightly around an empty gift box. Then she had to undo it to put the gift inside. For the next gift she packed and closed the box before tying its ribbon.","Olive described a complicated block pattern while her friend tried to remember every part. The copied pattern was different. Olive drew a small plan with each block’s place. Her friend used it to rebuild the pattern.","Omar cut up his only pattern while trying a new shape. When the new shape failed, he could not return to the first pattern. For his next trial he traced a spare copy and cut that copy instead.","Poppy compared two paper strips by holding one higher than the other. She chose the wrong longer strip. She laid them flat with their left ends together. Now she could see which strip reached farther.","Quinn covered the whole card with a thick puddle of glue. It soaked through and wrinkled the paper. On the next card she used a thin line only where the pieces joined. The card stayed flat.","Ravi spread his loose map pages on an outdoor bench. A gust blew two pages across the yard. He moved behind a closed window and spread them on an indoor table. The pages stayed where he put them.","Ren took every shelf out of a toy cupboard to clean it. Later she could not tell which shelf had fitted each space. Before cleaning the next cupboard, she put matching marks on the shelves and their spaces. They went back easily.","Sal wrote that the picnic would begin at ten, but left out the day. His cousin arrived on the wrong morning. Sal sent another note with both the day and the time, and his cousin came to the picnic.","Suri copied a striped flag and thought it was finished. When she held it beside the original, she noticed a missing white stripe. She added it, then compared the two flags once more.","Tariq kept searching the same three drawers for a missing stamp. He could not remember which ones he had checked. He placed an empty card beside each searched drawer and moved to the next one. He found the stamp in a new drawer.","Tess pushed all her seedlings into one corner of the tray. Their leaves overlapped and bent. She moved them farther apart into the empty spaces. The leaves no longer pressed against one another.","Zara pushed the same puzzle piece harder each time it would not fit. The cardboard began to bend. She stopped pushing, turned the piece, and found the position that matched the gap.","beach","bench","bud","c","cookie","crayon","dad","drum","elephant","face","fat","fed","foot","grap