ion/en-US/supplemental/watermelon-d3fb20877f.mp3","/images/assessment/generated/concepts/shout.webp","/images/assessment/generated/phonics-quality/wig.webp","/images/assessment/language/variants/verbs/bounce-01.webp","/images/assessment/language/variants/verbs/fold-01.webp","/images/assessment/language/variants/verbs/whisper-01.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-dig.webp","/images/assessment/literacy-mock/capacity/foundation-spill.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/nut.webp","/images/assessment/objective-words/run.webp","/images/assessment/release-media/umbrella-e1f6f2a3.webp","/images/assessment/release-support/targets/fog-dfebbd.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/bug/bug-02.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/eg/peg-02.webp","/images/assessment/rhyming/variants/in/bin-02.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/fork.webp","/images/child-mode/initial-sounds/hop.webp","/images/child-mode/short-i/sit.webp","/images/child-mode/vocabulary/fin.webp","/media/initial-sounds/images/b/basket.webp","/media/initial-sounds/images/p/pencil.webp","/media/initial-sounds/images/y/yam.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/bend.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/carry.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/chop.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/cop.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/cub.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/feed.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/gem.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/lift.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/march.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/peel.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/ride.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/roll.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/smell.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/stand.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/stir.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/verb-bake.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/verb-build.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/verb-cook.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/verb-drive.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/verb-pour.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/verb-shake.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/wear.webp","/media/vocabulary/images/yawn.webp","3","A copy is finished as soon as it looks close enough.","A large task can be tackled in smaller parts.","A person’s name begins with a capital wherever it appears in a sentence.","A player who loses should decide the new score.","A promised job can wait until somebody else notices it.","A quick guess is enough when things look familiar.","A simple record can preserve details we may forget.","A small job is never useful to the whole group.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group.","A stronger push is the best way to solve every problem.","A thing is free to use whenever its owner is away.","A visible guide can support a complicated explanation.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly.","Adding more decoration always makes a model work better.","Adding the most material always makes a better result.","Agree on a plan before working together.","Allow a change to finish before the next step.","Always change the only copy when trying a new idea.","Apply the stated prefix or suffix meaning to one root while rejecting two competing forms of that same root.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work.","Begin the next step while every surface is still wet.","Begin work before finding the tools you will need.","Being first matters more than waiting for other people.","Both alternatives split within a subject or predicate; all alternatives capitalize after the internal stop.","Changing your own note is enough to tell everyone a new plan.","Check identity instead of relying on a quick resemblance.","Check unclear directions before choosing what to do.","Check what another person can actually see.","Check what is true before acting on a guess.","Choose a manageable part and share work that is too much.","Choose a tool that fits the particular job.","Choose by the job a thing must do, not its looks.","Choose the best-looking material for every job.","Choose the first possible meaning of unclear directions.","Choose what looks best before asking what someone needs.","Compare finished work with its guide before moving on.","Complete printed and exact spoken context supports the affix contrast. Pictures would replace the required analysis of competing forms of the same root.","Cover every working part when you decorate a model.","Damage stops mattering when somebody puts it out of sight.","Decoration should leave the useful parts able to work.","Different starting points always give a fair comparison.","Different starting points make every race equally fair.","Do every part at once to make a large task easier.","Do needed earlier steps before starting later ones.","Eli","Empty spaces in someone’s work should always be filled in.","Explain unfamiliar routines so a newcomer can take part.","Explain your own mistake so it can be put right.","Find out what someone needs before making a choice.","Find the cause instead of repeating a temporary fix.","Gather the needed materials before beginning the job.","Give specific details when another person needs to find something.","Give useful guidance while leaving another person a chance to try.","Grandad","Help repair the damage when something goes wrong.","Helping means doing every hard step for the learner.","If one part works, every other part must work too.","Keep an earlier version when trying an uncertain change.","Keep every detail in your head instead of making notes.","Keep the first plan even when it does not work.","Leave enough space for things to work properly.","Leave out details so every instruction stays short.","Leave paper outside so there is more space to work.","Leave shared spaces clear for the people who need them.","Look for evidence before deciding what a problem means.","Make room for what is needed before adding extras.","Mina","Moving faster always makes the work more accurate.","New players should learn the rules by guessing alone.","One person should keep the best supplies for their own work.","One small container should hold everything you have.","One spoken explanation is always enough to copy every part.","One successful check does not check every part.","Only try a job after knowing that you will enjoy it.","Original affix-in-context contrasts with three real forms of one root; no NWEA items reused.","Plan how to carry out a job you have promised.","Protect work from the conditions that could damage it.","Puts a capital inside the word instead of using its conventional initial capital.","Quietly hiding a mistake is the best way to fix it.","Record the arrangement before taking something apart.","Repeat the same quick fix whenever the problem returns.","Repeating the same vague words always makes directions clear.","Required whole-word recordings identify the alternatives. Their spellings remain hidden; concrete illustrations support independent replay.","Return shared things to the place where others expect them.","Search in an order that avoids checking places repeatedly.","Search the same places again before looking anywhere new.","Share what is available so everyone can take part.","Shared tools should stay with the last person who used them.","Splits the first thought after its first word, leaving fragments.","Splits within the second thought rather than between the two complete thoughts.","Start the last step first to finish sooner.","Start with the whole job so no time is spent on tests.","Take care of useful supplies that other people share.","Take everything apart before deciding how it fits together.","Taking the biggest job alone always helps the group most.","Tell affected people when a plan changes.","Testing is only useful after all the work is done.","The best place to build is wherever there is empty floor.","The exact printed order and authored line break supply the evidence; the instruction never narrates the answer.","The first part of a message is all you need.","The first sign of a problem always tells you its cause.","The full stop separates two complete thoughts. Each new sentence starts with a capital.","The next person should deal with supplies left running.","The stronger partner should choose the plan for everyone.","Things that look alike must belong to the same person.","Things work best when they are packed tightly together.","This alternative does not meet the stated task. The first word of a sentence begins with a capital letter.","Track print from the end of one line back to the left edge of the following line.","Trust your first guess when the job seems easy.","Try a small test before doing the whole job.","Try an unfamiliar role before deciding it is not for you.","Use enough containers for the amount you have.","Use more force rather than changing a failed method.","Use one plan for everything, even when needs differ.","Use the amount needed instead of adding the most.","Use the biggest tool for every job.","Use the same conditions when making a fair comparison.","Use the same starting reference when comparing results.","Useful instructions need all the important details.","Wait for a clear turn when people share an activity.","What you can see must be clear to everyone else.","When a method fails, try a different approach.","Work alone so nobody needs to hear your problem.","a car’s storage space","a clear material for windows","a closure that keeps a lid shut","a container for a drink","a contest between players","a cover that closes a bottle","a curled piece of metal","a dog’s short loud sound","a field where a game is played","a flying animal","a greeting made with a hand","a kind of music","a kind of tree","a large bus for passengers","a learner at a school","a line of traffic that cannot move freely","a long-legged bird","a machine for lifting heavy loads","a machine that moves air","a metal fastener for wood","a particular day on a calendar","a person who supports a team","a person who trains a team","a piece of material 