soil.","Worms change soil by tunnelling and feeding.","Worms make new leaves grow on plants.","Worms pull fallen leaves beneath the ground.","Write a pattern title that describes its finished shape.","Write the owner’s name clearly on the book pocket.","Writing a complete list can help you remember everything to pack.","Young owls learn to leave their nests.","Yusuf counted how long two toy cars rolled, but started counting at different moments. His numbers did not compare the full journeys. He rolled them again and began counting at the start line each time.","Zara","a basin","a bee visits flowers for nectar to take to its hive. pollen sticks to its body during these visits. some pollen reaches another flower when the bee lands there, helping that plant make seeds while the bee collects its food.","a blanket","a board at our bus stop shows when each bus is due. people use it to decide whether to wait or walk. a roof and side panels keep the waiting seats dry during rain.","a bowl","a bucket caught the drips from the ceiling.","a bucket","a camera","a closed gate keeps footballs out of the young plants in our school garden. along the beds, wide paths leave room for visitors to walk and look without stepping on the soil. classes open the gate when their visit begins.","a duck’s soft inner feathers trap warm air near its body. it spreads oil over its outer feathers, which helps water roll off. these different layers protect the duck when it swims in cold water.","a group decorated a cart but left its loose wheel unfixed. the cart could not carry their bags until they repaired it. for a birthday, ari spent all his coins on wrapping paper and could not buy the card he needed. next time he chose the card first and used the coins left over for wrapping paper.","a mask","a model castle blocked the classroom doorway and people bumped it. the builders moved it onto a side table. at the reading corner, bags covered every seat. rina put them on hooks, and children could sit down with their books.","a model castle filled the classroom doorway. people bumped it when they entered. the builders moved it onto a side table, and people could walk through without touching it.","a narrow footbridge lets walkers cross our river without waiting. it cannot carry vehicles. a ferry farther downstream has room for vans and takes them across with their heavier loads.","a net","a new child ran the wrong way because the group had not explained their game. they showed her and practised a slow round. in class, a new pupil stayed standing when a silent signal meant sit down. a partner showed what the signal meant before the next activity.","a parent","a pupil","a saucepan","a scarf","a sheet","a teacher","a torch","a towel","a toy blocks light from a torch. moving the torch to one side shifts the shadow to the other side. moving the toy closer to the torch makes its shadow larger. the same toy can make different shadows without changing its own shape.","a visitor greeted the host after pinning on a badge. she had left her bag before pinning on the badge.","a visitor returned the lost mitten.","a visitor","a worker tests the swings and checks the climbing frame before the playground opens. if a part is loose, she puts a barrier around that equipment. she writes the fault on a repair sheet for the repair team.","above the door","above the shoe rack","ada fixed the tear before the play began.","ada hung the picture list above her own head. the younger children could not see what to collect. she crouched beside them, noticed the shelf in their way, and moved the list down where they could see it. jin explained the model while holding its opening toward himself. his partner could not see the part he named. jin moved around to his partner’s side and turned the model. the opening was now visible to both of them.","ada hung the picture list above her own head. the younger children could not see what to collect. she crouched beside them, noticed the shelf in their way, and moved the list down where they could see it.","ada rushed her folds and tore a paper bird. she slowed down at the difficult folds on the next one. malik rushed to announce a game score and read the wrong line. he paused to check the names before announcing the next score.","ada rushed to fold a paper bird and tore a wing. she slowed down at each fold on the next bird, which stayed whole.","adapt","afraid","after using the magnifier, sol left it in his coat. the nature group searched the shelf and could not start. sol returned it to its labelled place, where the next group found it.","alma poured paint onto a mixing plate and then went to find a brush and water. the paint dried while she searched. before her next painting she put the brush, water and plate together, then poured the paint. sam started building the puppet stage before checking its fasteners. he held two walls up for a long time while a friend searched for clips. next time he collected the clips and walls together before joining the stage.","alma poured paint onto a mixing plate and then went to find a brush and water. the paint dried while she searched. before her next painting she put the brush, water and plate together, then poured the paint.","along the path","amir took a blue coat from the hook because it looked like his. its owner came looking for it. amir checked the name inside and returned it. then he checked another blue coat and found his own name. ivy carried a seed packet to the bean bed because its picture looked like beans. the gardener showed her that it was a pea packet. ivy read the names on the remaining packets before taking the bean seeds.","amir took a blue coat from the hook because it looked like his. its owner came looking for it. amir checked the name inside and returned it. then he checked another blue coat and found his own name.","an owl’s large eyes help it see in dim light. its hearing helps it locate small animals it cannot easily see. soft feather edges make its flight quiet as it approaches prey at night.","angry names a different action, feeling or property; it does not mean scared.","arun moved the screen after naming the puppet. he had opened a bag before naming it.","asha moved the meeting blanket from the tree to the porch when rain began. her friend kept waiting under the tree. asha went back and explained the change. her friend brought his bag to the dry porch. max changed the class shop’s opening time on his own note. the helpers arrived at the old time. before changing it again, he spoke to each helper and changed the shared sign. they arrived together.","asha moved the meeting blanket from the tree to the porch when rain began. her friend kept waiting under the tree. asha went back and explained the change. her friend brought his bag to the dry porch.","at book swap, volunteers collect books that families have finished reading. they put books with missing pages aside. other volunteers ask visitors what they enjoy and help them choose a book to take home.","at the animal shelter, morning helpers refill the food and water bowls. they tick each completed job on a chart. afternoon helpers read the chart and check what has been done before starting their own jobs.","at the drinking station, a high tap leaves room for a bottle underneath. children can fill their bottles without tipping them sideways. spilled water runs through holes in a tray instead of collecting on the floor.","at the returns desk, a helper scans each book to clear its loan. readers can then borrow something else. the returned books go on labelled trolleys so another helper can take them to the right shelves.","at the sports centre, a timetable shows which room each class uses. families check it before going upstairs. a board beside it lists classes with spare places, so visitors can choose something new to join.","ava pulled a shared picture book from beneath a pile and tore its cover. she showed the teacher the tear and helped attach a new cover. the book returned to the shelf.","ava tore the cover of a shared book. she helped the teacher attach a new cover before returning it. leo knocked over a class plant and broke its pot. he helped move the plant into a spare pot and cleaned up the fallen soil.","bea could not lift a large box, so she carried its loose lids while others carried it. at a display, ren could not paint the large pictures and sat aside. he made clear name labels, and visitors could tell which group had made each picture.","bea could not lift the large box and thought she could not help. she carried the loose lids while two others carried the box. the whole set reached the hall together.","bea fetched some paper after drawing a line. she had washed a brush before drawing the line.","bea filled the jug after folding the napkins. she had chosen the dish before folding the napkins.","bea forgot which seeds she had sown. she labelled the next pots so she could care for each plant correctly.","before choosing a book, noor stacked the cushions. she had stroked the cat before stacking the cushions.","before choosing a pear, lina lifted her basket. she had counted her coins before lifting the basket.","before cooking, our class reads the recipe and measures its ingredients into bowls. this makes it easy to find each amount when needed. after cooking, we wash the tools and wipe the worktops ready for the next group.","before drying her shoes, tess folded the map. before folding the map, she counted the birds.","before our walking group leaves, the leader counts everyone and checks the list of names. at each crossing she waits until the whole group is together. a helper at the back tells her if someone needs to stop.","before packing his notebook, arun tied his scarf. before tying his scarf, he waved a flag.","before photographing the jetty, finn put away his hat. before putting away his hat, he handed over his ticket.","before putting on his hat, eli sharpened his pencil. before sharpening the pencil, h