ore the child below had moved away. they nearly bumped. jem waited for the bottom to clear on his next turn, and both children had room.","jo gave every plant the same water. one pot stayed soggy. she checked its soil and watered it less, and it grew stronger.","jo kept the game scores in her head. after a break she could not remember which team had seven points. on the next game she marked every point on a scorecard. the teams could check the score after the break. mateo lent out the class puppets without writing down the borrowers. at tidy-up he did not know who still had one. next time he wrote each name beside a puppet picture and ticked it when the puppet returned.","jo kept the game scores in her head. after a break she could not remember which team had seven points. on the next game she marked every point on a scorecard. the teams could check the score after the break.","jo tied her shoe after checking the score. she had carried the hoop before checking the score.","jo watered every plant alike until one stayed soggy. she changed its watering to suit the soil. sal gave everyone the same job in a play; a quiet child struggled to announce scenes. sal offered a backstage job that suited the child better.","jun wrapped the drum in a blanket.","kai switched on the torch after putting down the bag. he had put down the bag after unfolding the blanket.","kai used a wide cup to pour beads into a narrow bottle. beads bounced onto the floor. he held a funnel in the neck and poured through it. the beads went into the bottle. lena used a thick brush to paint the tiny windows on her model. paint covered the wall around each window. she changed to a thin brush and painted the remaining windows without covering the walls.","kai used a wide cup to pour beads into a narrow bottle. beads bounced onto the floor. he held a funnel in the neck and poured through it. the beads went into the bottle.","kettle","kim scattered the board after losing. she helped set it up and asked for a