ised fish-feeding job while playing. the next day she fed the fish before her game and marked the chart. finn promised to bring a banner but left it at home. for the next event he put the finished banner beside his school bag the night before.","noor promised to feed the class fish but joined a game and forgot. the teacher fed them. the next day noor did the feeding job before joining the game and marked it on the chart.","noor repaired the model’s roof. eli watched her work.","noor tied the ribbon tightly around an empty gift box. then she had to undo it to put the gift inside. for the next gift she packed and closed the box before tying its ribbon. leo mixed a batch of plaster before making a space for the mold. while he searched for a clear tray, the mixture became too stiff to pour. for the next batch he set out the mold and tray before mixing.","noor tied the ribbon tightly around an empty gift box. then she had to undo it to put the gift inside. for the next gift she packed and closed the box before tying its ribbon.","note","oli took all the gold stickers, leaving his group none. he returned the sheet and they divided them. at games club, may kept the board game for the whole session, leaving others no turn. next time she agreed to pass it to another pair after ten minutes.","oli took the whole sheet of gold stickers for his crown. his group had none left. he returned the sheet, and they divided the stickers before finishing everyone’s crowns.","olive described a complicated block pattern while her friend tried to remember every part. the copied pattern was different. olive drew a small plan with each block’s place. her friend used it to rebuild the pattern. dev called out the drum rhythm once and expected the group to remember it. they stopped at different places. he drew a row of beat marks and pointed along them. the group could follow the same rhythm.","olive described a complicated block pattern while her friend tried to remember every part. the copied pattern was different. olive drew a small plan with each block’s place. her friend used it to rebuild the pattern.","omar cut up his only pattern while trying a new shape. when the new shape failed, he could not return to the first pattern. for his next trial he traced a spare copy and cut that copy instead. cleo changed the only written plan for her puppet scene and later forgot the earlier ending. before her next change, she copied the plan onto another sheet. she could compare both endings and choose one.","omar cut up his only pattern while trying a new shape. when the new shape failed, he could not return to the first pattern. for his next trial he traced a spare copy and cut that copy instead.","on the court","on the playground floor","on the shelf","on top of the carpet","only_not_sufficient","open","opening the tin happens before tying the bow, which happens before counting the tickets; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","our class draws the sky and records the temperature each morning. each page has a date. on friday we lay the pages together to find which mornings were warmer and which had rain.","our picnic cart has deep sides to stop baskets slipping off. straps hold the drinks upright while it moves. its large wheels roll over the bumpy grass between the gate and our picnic spot.","outside the jacket pocket","overfilled","own","packed","packing her cup happens before watching the bird, which happens before zipping the bag; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","pain","palm","passing out the shakers happens before ringing the bell, which happens before moving the stool; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","patch","picture maps at the welcome desk show the rooms in our school. visitors can follow the marked route to a classroom. helpers also answer questions about lessons and clubs that are not shown on the maps.","pipe","pitch","plane","plants around a pond provide hiding places for frogs. insects near the water provide 