 and their spaces. they went back easily.","ren tried carrying a heavy crate alone and could not lift it clear of the floor. he asked a helper to carry the other end. together they moved it onto the trolley.","repacked","rested","rig","rina carried the empty tray upstairs.","roots hold a plant upright and take in water. some also store food for later growth. these jobs happen below the ground, although their effects reach the stem and leaves.","rotating the globe happens before stacking the cards, which happens before closing the atlas; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","sal wrote that the picnic would begin at ten, but left out the day. his cousin arrived on the wrong morning. sal sent another note with both the day and the time, and his cousin came to the picnic. pia copied that the model needed three strips, but left out their length. her group cut strips too short for the roof. she checked the plan and wrote both the number and the length. the new strips reached across.","sal wrote that the picnic would begin at ten, but left out the day. his cousin arrived on the wrong morning. sal sent another note with both the day and the time, and his cousin came to the picnic.","sam watered the plants while jo was away.","scared and afraid mean about the same.","scared","seal","seven flags lined the path to the hall.","sewing the puppet’s hat happens before moving the screen, which happens before closing the box; the account opens by mentioning a later event.","shin","short","signs above the stairs show which platforms are below. travellers follow the number printed on their tickets. when a train changes platform, staff at the information desk explain the change and point out the new route.","six empty baskets stood beside the fruit stall.","six flowering plants grew inside the greenhouse.","small pockets keep pencils away from the books in our backpack. wide shoulder straps spread the weight while we carry it. a buckle lets us shorten the straps when the bag