_synonyms:synonym_picture","@prefix_suffix:apply_affix_meaning_in_context","A MITTEN FELL BEHIND THE BENCH.","A PARCEL ARRIVED FOR OMAR.","A SNAIL LEFT A SILVER TRAIL.","A banana is a fruit.","A bear sleeps through winter.","A board at our bus stop shows when each bus is due.","A board beside it lists classes with spare places, so visitors can choose something new to join.","A closed gate keeps footballs out of the young plants in our school garden.","A crane stood on long legs in the pond, spreading its wings before it flew away. Across the road, a building crane lifted steel beams with a long arm and hook.","A dog gave a loud bark when Arun opened the gate. Arun then touched the rough bark covering the tree’s trunk.","A ferry farther downstream has room for vans and takes them across with their heavier loads.","A group decorated a cart but left its loose wheel unfixed. The cart could not carry their bags until they repaired it.","A helper at the back tells her if someone needs to stop.","A lantern lit the dark path.","A large task can be tackled in smaller parts. Each other choice explains one episode, while this lesson explains both.","A large task can be tackled in smaller parts. It explains the mistake-to-repair change in both episodes.","A large task can be tackled in smaller parts. It explains the mistake-to-repair change.","A large task can be tackled in smaller parts. The changed action resolves the problem in this episode.","A metal clip held the two sheets together so they did not blow away. On her tablet, Mina played a short clip that showed a bird taking off, then stopped after a few seconds.","A model castle blocked the classroom doorway and people bumped it. The builders moved it onto a side table.","A mouse nibbles a seed.","A narrow footbridge lets walkers cross our river without waiting.","A neighbor brought the lost puppy home. Its owner wanted to express thanks.","A new child ran the wrong way because the group had not explained their game. They showed her and practised a slow round.","A printed programme names the characters and lists the scenes so families can follow the play.","A repair basket holds clothes with loose buttons or tears, and a helper mends them before the next show.","A roof and side panels keep the waiting seats dry during rain.","A runner refused to congratulate the winner after a race. Later he shook the winner’s hand and joined her for practice before the next race.","A seal swam past the boat and dived under the water. Back home, Kit broke the seal around the jar’s lid before opening it.","A simple record can preserve details we may forget. Each other choice explains one episode, while this lesson explains both.","A simple record can preserve details we may forget. It explains the mistake-to-repair change in both episodes.","A simple record can preserve details we may forget. It explains the mistake-to-repair change.","A simple record can preserve details we may forget. The changed action resolves the problem in this episode.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","A smaller useful job can still help the whole group. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","A tall palm had a ringed trunk and long leaves above the beach. Jo held a shell on her open palm, between her fingers and her wrist.","A tiny root appeared. We drew it in our notebook.","A truck carries the heavy boxes.","A visible guide can support a complicated explanation. Each other choice explains one episode, while this lesson explains both.","A visible guide can support a complicated explanation. It explains the mistake-to-repair change in both episodes.","A visible guide can support a complicated explanation. It explains the mistake-to-repair change.","A visible guide can support a complicated explanation. The changed action resolves the problem in this episode.","A visitor greeted the host after pinning on a badge.","A wooden post held up one end of the fence. Later, the post arrived in a bag of letters that the carrier left at our door.","A worker tests the swings and checks the climbing frame before the playground opens.","AFTER","ALI","AMIR","ARLO","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Accept a result and keep treating other players kindly. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Acts on the original guess even though the soil is already wet.","Acts on the untested guess and risks discarding the puppet shoes.","Adds a load before correcting the fault that prevents the cart carrying it.","Adds speed without settling the disagreement about where the bridge should go.","After cooking, we wash the tools and wipe the worktops ready for the next group.","After running, I could feel my heart beating inside my chest. I sat beside a wooden chest with a hinged lid and blankets inside.","After","Afternoon helpers read the chart and check what has been done before starting their own jobs.","Agree on a plan before working together. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Agree on a plan before working together. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Allow a change to finish before the next step. Each other choice explains one episode, while this lesson explains both.","Allow a change to finish before the next step. It explains the mistake-to-repair change in both episodes.","Allow a change to finish before the next step. It explains the mistake-to-repair change.","Allow a change to finish before the next step. The changed action resolves the problem in this episode.","Along the beds, wide paths leave room for visitors to walk and look without stepping on the soil.","An elephant has a long trunk.","Ana shared her lunch with someone who had forgotten theirs.","Another helper compares the parcels with an order list and asks about anything missing.","Arun called his hat lost when he found its peg empty. A notice said damp clothes had been moved to the drying rack. He checked the rack and found his hat.","Arun touched the rough bark covering the tree’s trunk.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Ask before using something that belongs to another person. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work. Each narrower alternative fits only one of the two episodes.","Ask what help is wanted before changing someone’s work. The changed action resolves the problem in the supplied story.","At a display, Ren could not paint the large pictures and sat aside. He made clear name labels, and visitors could tell which group had made each picture.","At a match, Mae wrote an extra goal for her team. She told the referee about her error, and the score was corrected before the next game.","At book swap, volunteers collect books that families have finished reading.","At games club, May kept the board game for the whole session, leaving others no turn. Next time she agreed to pass it to another pair after ten minutes.","At music club, May rejected the shaker because she had not played it before. She tried one short rhythm and asked to play it again with the song.","At music club, an older player played a beginner’s part as well as his own. He offered a starting cue instead, and the beginner played the short part herself.","At music club, two children struck the same drum at once and knocked sticks together. They agreed to play one short turn each.","At playtime, Ari thought a quiet newcomer wanted to be alone. Ari asked, and learned that the child wanted to play but did not know the rules.","At the animal shelter, morning helpers refill the food and water bowls.","At the craft table, Bo threw away large clean paper pieces after cutting small stars. He took the pieces back out and left them in a tray for another group’s drawings.","At the drinking station, a high tap leaves room for a bottle underneath.","At the end, Ada put on her scarf.","At the end, Arun closed the bag.","At the end, Arun folded the flag.","At the end, Bea emptied the jug.","At the end, Bea put away the brush.","At the end, Bo put stamps on the cards.","At the end, Dad folded the blanket.","At the end, Dad put away his bottle.","At the end, Dad took the bear off the bed.","At the end, Eli drew a butterfly.","At the end, Eve collected the menus.","At the end, Finn collected his ticket.","At the end, Jo put away the hoop.","At the end, Kai folded the blanket.","At the end, Kit took off the hat.","At the end, Kit unpacked her cup.","At the end, Lina paid for the pear.","At the end, May put away the chair.","At the end, Mina cut up the apples.","At the end, Nia took down a photo.","At the end, Noor put the book away.","At the end, Ren opened the atlas.","At the end, Ren put away the cards.","At the end, Sal opened the window.","At the end, Sol opened his bag.","At the end, Tess opened another book.","At the end, Tess opened the map.","At the end, Uma put on her gloves.","At the end, bright arrows point back to the car park so people can find their return route.","At the end, the actors started the fan.","At the end, the baker put away the flour.","At the end, the children put away the shakers.","At the end, the class planted the seeds.","At the end, the class put away the drums.","At the end, the class rubbed out the line.","At the end, the cyclist put on his helmet.","At the end, the group packed away the pencils.","At the end, the group put away the bags.","At the end, the group took down the plan.","At the end, the helper closed the tin.","At the end, the keeper opened the animal gate.","At the end, the nurse fed the puppy.","At the end, the players unpacked the puppet’s clothes.","At the end, the potter dried the clay.","At the end, the teacher opened the register.","At the end, the visitor took off the badge.","At the named occurrence, cap means a cover that closes a bottle.","At the named occurrence, chest means a storage box with a lid.","At the named occurrence, clip means a small fastener that holds things together.","At the named occurrence, coach means a person who trains a team.","At the named occurrence, crane means a long-legged bird.","At the named occurrence, date means a particular day on a calendar.","At the named occurrence, fan means a machine that moves air.","At the named occurrence, jam means a line of traffic that cannot move freely.","At the named occurrence, letter means a written message sent to someone.","At the named occurrence, nail means a metal fastener for wood.","At the named occurrence, palm means a kind of tree.","At the named occurrence, patch means a piece of material covering a hole.","At the named occurrence, pitch means a field where a game is played.","At the named occurrence, post means letters delivered to a home.","At the named occurrence, pupil means a learner at a school.","At the named occurrence, rock means a solid stone material.","At the queried occurrence, \"bank\" means the edge of a river.","At the queried occurrence, \"bark\" means a tree’s outer covering.","At the queried occurrence, \"bat\" means a flying animal.","At the queried occurrence, \"glass\" means a container for a drink.","At the queried occurrence, \"match\" means a contest between players.","At the queried occurrence, \"ring\" means jewellery worn on a finger.","At the queried occurrence, \"seal\" means a closure that keeps a lid shut.","At the queried occurrence, \"spring\" means a curled piece of metal.","At the queried occurrence, \"trunk\" means the main stem of a tree.","At the queried occurrence, \"wave\" means a greeting made with a hand.","At the reading corner, bags covered every seat. Rina put them on hooks, and children could sit down with their books.","At the returns desk, a helper scans each bo