ated relation in this entry passage.","“Choose a map large enough for the group to share.” does not explain this correction. The wind scattered loose pages, and moving indoors sheltered them; map size and route coverage would not stop the gust.","“Choose a picnic place with room for everyone.” does not explain this correction. The note left out the day, causing an arrival on the wrong morning; an envelope or larger picnic site would not supply the missing day.","“Choose a puzzle with enough pieces for everyone.” does not explain this correction. Pushing bent the puzzle piece, while turning it revealed the fit; sorting colors or sharing pieces would not change the failing method.","“Choose a wider block to push through the gap.” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“Choose card colors that stand out against the wall.” does not explain this correction. Excess glue soaked and wrinkled the card; the card colors and the storage tray would not reduce that excess.","“Choose clear pictures of the objects to collect.” does not explain this correction. The younger children could not see past the shelf; strong paper and clear pictures would not move the list into their view.","“Choose colors that make a toy cart easy to find.” does not explain this correction. Wrapping jammed a moving wheel; attractive colors and a comfortable handle would not clear the wheel.","“Choose colors that make the model’s shape easy to see.” does not explain this correction. The attractive thin base bent under the load; visible colors and display measurements would not make that base stiff enough.","“Choose fabric that will move freely in the wind.” does not explain this correction. Comparison revealed a missing stripe after Suri thought she had finished; fabric movement and the display pole would not reveal that omission.","“Choose flag colors that visitors can see clearly.” does not explain this correction. The flag paint cracked because it had not been tried on spare paper; separating colors or making flags visible would not test that paint.","“Choose paint colors that show against the background.” does not explain this correction. The paint dried while Alma searched for tools; color contrast and protecting a finished picture would not have put the tools ready beforehand.","“Choose plant labels that can survive getting wet.” does not explain this correction. The seedlings pressed against one another because they were crowded; labels and counting would not leave room between the leaves.","“Choose plants that fit the space on a shelf.” does not explain this correction. The same puddle returned because the tray was cracked; plant size and dividing watering jobs would not repair the leak.","“Choose scissors suited to the thickness of the paper.” does not explain this correction. Cutting the only pattern removed the earlier version; suitable scissors and a title would not preserve an uncut copy.","“Choose scissors that can cut the paper strips cleanly.” does not explain this correction. Holding the strips at different starting positions gave a misleading comparison; cutting tools and storage would not align their ends.","“Choose strong paper for a pocket that holds books.” does not explain this correction. The pocket was too narrow for the actual book; strong paper and an owner name would not establish the required size.","“Choose teams with equal numbers of players.” does not explain this correction. Jo forgot the score after a break and used written marks to retain it; team size and practice time would not preserve the score.","“Choose the quickest watering plan for every pot.” does not answer the stated relation in this entry passage.","“Choose wrapping that is large enough for the box.” does not explain this correction. The empty box had been tied before the gift was inside, so the ribbon had to be undone; wrapping size and gift choice would not correct that order.","“Count the seedlings before carrying a full tray.” does not explain t